Ques:-

The Nautilus DevOps team needs to create an AMI from an existing instance for backup and scaling purposes. 
They have an existing EC2 instance named xfusion-ec2 and need to create an AMI named xfusion-ec2-ami from this instance. 
Additionally, they need to launch a new EC2 instance named xfusion-ec2-new using this AMI.




Soln:-

Step 1:- Identify the Instance ID

aws ec2 describe-instances --filters "Name=tag:Name,Values=<existing-instance-name>"



Step 2:- Create the AMI

aws ec2 create-image --instance-id <id> --name "<new AMI name>" --description "AMI created from xfusion-ec2 instance" --no-reboot



Step 3:- Verify AMI Creation

aws ec2 describe-images --image-ids <AMI_ID>



Step 4:- Create the key pair

aws ec2 create-key-pair \
    --key-name <keypair-name> \
    --query 'KeyMaterial' \
    --output text > <keypair-name>
	
	
	
Step 5:- Secure the private key file

chmod 400 <keypair-name>.pem



Step 6:- Use the key pair when launching an instance

aws ec2 run-instances \
    --image-id <AMI_ID> \
    --count 1 \
    --instance-type t2.micro \
    --key-name <keypair-name> \
    --tag-specifications 'ResourceType=instance,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=<new-instance-name>}]'
	
	
	
Step 7:- Verification of the New Instance

aws ec2 describe-instances \
    --filters "Name=tag:Name,Values=<instance-name>" \
    --query "Reservations[*].Instances[*].PublicIpAddress" \
    --output text
